{"name":"Blue Earth","hex":"#375673","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Blue Earth","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city, the county seat of Faribault County, Minnesota, United States. Named after the Blue Earth River."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Blue_Earth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Earth, Minnesota","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Earth is a city in Faribault County, Minnesota, United States, at the confluence of the east and west branches of the Blue Earth River. The population was 3,174 at the 2020 census. It is the county seat of Faribault County. It is home to a statue of the Jolly Green Giant. Additionally, Interstate 90 is centered on Blue Earth, as the east and west construction teams met here in 1978. As a tribute, there is a golden stripe of concrete on the interstate near Blue Earth. This draws an analogy to the golden spike set in the first transcontinental railroad. Approximately three miles south of Blue Earth is the Blue Earth Municipal Airport."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Blue_Earth%2C_Minnesota.jpg/330px-Blue_Earth%2C_Minnesota.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Earth%2C_Minnesota"},{"title":"Blue Earth City Township, Faribault County, Minnesota","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Earth City Township is a township in Faribault County, Minnesota, United States. The population was 454 at the 2000 census."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Earth_City_Township%2C_Faribault_County%2C_Minnesota"},{"title":"Blue Earth (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Earth is a studio album by American alt country and alt rock band the Jayhawks, released in 1989."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/82/Blue_Earth_Jayhawks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Earth_(album)"},{"title":"Earth","blocks":[{"text":"Earth is the third planet from the Sun and the only astronomical object known to harbor life. This is made possible by Earth being an ocean world, the only one in the Solar System sustaining liquid surface water. Almost all of Earth's water is contained in its ocean, which covers 70.8% of Earth's crust. The remaining 29.2% of Earth's crust is dry land, which is predominantly located within Earth's land hemisphere in the form of continental landmasses. Most of Earth's land is at least somewhat humid and covered by vegetation, while large ice sheets at Earth's polar deserts retain more water than Earth's groundwater, lakes, rivers, and atmospheric water combined. Earth's crust consists of slowly moving tectonic plates, which interact to produce mountain ranges, volcanoes, and earthquakes. Earth has a liquid outer core that generates a magnetosphere capable of deflecting most of the destructive solar winds and cosmic radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Meteosat-12-fci-march-equinox-2025-noon.jpg/330px-Meteosat-12-fci-march-equinox-2025-noon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earth"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Jolly_Green_Giant_Statue.jpg/500px-Jolly_Green_Giant_Statue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Jolly_Green_Giant_Statue.jpg/1280px-Jolly_Green_Giant_Statue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Jolly_Green_Giant_Statue.jpg/500px-Jolly_Green_Giant_Statue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Jolly Green Giant statue is 55.5' (17 m) tall","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJolly_Green_Giant_Statue.jpg"},{"srcset":"https: